  "id": "hercynian-coastal-foreland",
  "name": "Hercynian Coastal Foreland",
  "zoneNumber": 1,
  "description": "Humid warm-temperate/subtropical coastal foreland between the northern sea and the Hercynian uplands. Mixed open woodland and grassland dominate, with abundant rivers and wet valleys; localized wetlands and wet woodland occupy low ground, while exposed ridges are drier. The western boundary transitions rapidly toward arid country and the eastern boundary toward savannah.",
